From 071a78e07cb68a0a4babc8325c014ba72a22507b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add window.splash manifest field for a startup splash

Document the new `window.splash` field. It is a page or image (or
{url, width, height, min_duration, transparent}) shown in a frameless,
centered, always-on-top window while the main window loads. The main
window is then shown and the splash closed. The window bootstrap
scripts live in nwjs/chromium.src (chrome/browser/resources/nwjs/
newwin.js and default.js) and are changed in the companion commit
there.

In this repo:
- add the `splash` manifest key constant and keep it out of the
  attributes inherited by windows opened from the app
- document the field in Manifest Format.md
- add sanity tests for an HTML splash (size, min_duration, main window
  shown afterwards) and an image splash (auto-sized to the image,
  together with "show": false)

Fixes #151
